## Data Model

### Supported Data Types

```
String (S)
- Text data
- Example: "John Doe", "user@example.com"

Number (N)
- Integers and decimals
- Example: 42, 3.14

Binary (B)
- Encrypted data, images
- Example: Binary file content

Boolean
- True or false values
- Example: true, false

Null
- Empty/missing value
- Example: null

String Set (SS)
- Multiple string values
- Example: ["red", "blue", "green"]

Number Set (NS)
- Multiple number values
- Example: [1, 2, 3]

Binary Set (BS)
- Multiple binary values
- Example: [binary1, binary2]

Map (M)
- Nested document structure
- Example: { "address": { "city": "NYC", "zip": "10001" } }

List (L)
- Ordered array of values
- Example: ["item1", 42, true, {"key": "value"}]
```

