## Consistency Models

### 1. Strongly Consistent Read (SCR)
- Returns most up-to-date data
- All replicas updated before response
- Higher latency
- Uses 2x read capacity

```bash
# Strongly Consistent Read
aws dynamodb get-item \
  --table-name Users \
  --key '{"user_id":{"S":"user-123"}}' \
  --consistent-read
```

### 2. Eventually Consistent Read (ECR) - Default
- May return stale data (typically <1 second)
- Lower latency
- Uses standard read capacity
- Default for most queries

```bash
# Eventually Consistent Read (default)
aws dynamodb get-item \
  --table-name Users \
  --key '{"user_id":{"S":"user-123"}}'
```

**When to Use:**
- SCR: Financial transactions, inventory, user profiles
- ECR: Analytics, recommendations, non-critical data

