## Indexing

### 1. Global Secondary Index (GSI)

**Characteristics:**
- Different partition key from table
- Can have different sort key
- Can be created/deleted anytime
- Eventual consistency by default
- Separate capacity units

```bash
# Create table with GSI
aws dynamodb create-table \
  --table-name Users \
  --attribute-definitions \
    AttributeName=user_id,AttributeType=S \
    AttributeName=email,AttributeType=S \
  --key-schema \
    AttributeName=user_id,KeyType=HASH \
  --global-secondary-indexes \
    IndexName=EmailIndex,\
    Keys=[{AttributeName=email,KeyType=HASH}],\
    Projection={ProjectionType=ALL},\
    ProvisionedThroughput={ReadCapacityUnits=5,WriteCapacityUnits=5} \
  --billing-mode PROVISIONED \
  --provisioned-throughput ReadCapacityUnits=10,WriteCapacityUnits=10

# Query by email using GSI
aws dynamodb query \
  --table-name Users \
  --index-name EmailIndex \
  --key-condition-expression "email = :email" \
  --expression-attribute-values '{":email":{"S":"john@example.com"}}'
```

### 2. Local Secondary Index (LSI)

**Characteristics:**
- Same partition key as table
- Different sort key
- Must be created at table creation time
- Limited to 10 GB per partition key value
- Strong consistency option available

```bash
# Create table with LSI
aws dynamodb create-table \
  --table-name Orders \
  --attribute-definitions \
    AttributeName=user_id,AttributeType=S \
    AttributeName=order_id,AttributeType=S \
    AttributeName=created_at,AttributeType=S \
  --key-schema \
    AttributeName=user_id,KeyType=HASH \
    AttributeName=order_id,KeyType=RANGE \
  --local-secondary-indexes \
    IndexName=CreatedAtIndex,\
    Keys=[{AttributeName=user_id,KeyType=HASH},{AttributeName=created_at,KeyType=RANGE}],\
    Projection={ProjectionType=ALL} \
  --billing-mode PROVISIONED \
  --provisioned-throughput ReadCapacityUnits=10,WriteCapacityUnits=10

# Query orders by user and creation date
aws dynamodb query \
  --table-name Orders \
  --index-name CreatedAtIndex \
  --key-condition-expression "user_id = :uid AND created_at BETWEEN :start AND :end" \
  --expression-attribute-values '{
    ":uid":{"S":"user-123"},
    ":start":{"S":"2025-01-01T00:00:00Z"},
    ":end":{"S":"2025-12-31T23:59:59Z"}
  }'
```

