## Advanced Features

### 1. DynamoDB Streams

```bash
# Enable streams on table
aws dynamodb update-table \
  --table-name Users \
  --stream-specification StreamEnabled=true,StreamViewType=NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES

# Stream view types:
# - KEYS_ONLY: Only key attributes
# - NEW_IMAGE: New item image
# - OLD_IMAGE: Old item image  
# - NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES: Both new and old

# Lambda function triggered by stream
# Processes database changes in real-time
```

### 2. Global Tables (Multi-Region Replication)

```bash
# Create global table (replica in us-west-2)
aws dynamodb create-global-table \
  --global-table-name Users \
  --replication-group RegionName=us-east-1 RegionName=us-west-2

# Enable automatic replication between regions
# Read/write from any region
# Automatic failover
```

### 3. Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR)

```bash
# Enable PITR
aws dynamodb update-continuous-backups \
  --table-name Users \
  --point-in-time-recovery-specification PointInTimeRecoveryEnabled=true

# Restore to point in time
aws dynamodb restore-table-to-point-in-time \
  --source-table-name Users \
  --target-table-name Users-Restored \
  --restore-date-time 2025-11-25T10:00:00Z
```

### 4. Backup and Restore

```bash
# Create on-demand backup
aws dynamodb create-backup \
  --table-name Users \
  --backup-name Users-Backup-20251125

# List backups
aws dynamodb list-backups --table-name Users

# Restore from backup
aws dynamodb restore-table-from-backup \
  --target-table-name Users-Restored \
  --backup-arn arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-1:123456789012:table/Users/backup/01699632000000-12345678
```

