## Troubleshooting

### Problem 1: Throttling (Request Rate Too High)

**Error:** `ProvisionedThroughputExceededException` or `RequestLimitExceeded`

**Solution:**
```bash
# Check consumed capacity
aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \
  --namespace AWS/DynamoDB \
  --metric-name ConsumedWriteCapacityUnits \
  --dimensions Name=TableName,Value=Users \
  --start-time 2025-11-25T00:00:00Z \
  --end-time 2025-11-25T23:59:59Z \
  --period 300 \
  --statistics Sum

# Increase provisioned capacity
aws dynamodb update-table \
  --table-name Users \
  --provisioned-throughput ReadCapacityUnits=50,WriteCapacityUnits=50

# Or switch to on-demand
aws dynamodb update-table-billing-mode \
  --table-name Users \
  --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST

# Implement exponential backoff in application
```

### Problem 2: Hot Partitions (Uneven Data Distribution)

**Symptoms:** Some requests throttled while capacity available

**Solution:**
```bash
# Add random suffix to partition key
# Original: user_id: "user-123"
# Better: partition_key: "user-123#shard-001" (distribute across shards)

# Use DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) for caching
# Add GSI with different partition key
# Implement request sharding application-side
```

### Problem 3: Slow Queries

**Symptoms:** Query latency higher than expected

**Solution:**
```bash
# Check if using scan instead of query
# Query: Specify partition key (efficient)
# Scan: Reads all items (inefficient)

# Enable query logging
# Review CloudWatch metrics
# Check filter expressions (apply after reading)
# Use projections to reduce data transfer

# Implement caching with DAX
aws dynamodb create-cluster \
  --cluster-name MyDAXCluster \
  --iam-role-arn arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/DAXServiceRole \
  --node-type dax.r5.large \
  --replication-factor 3
```

### Problem 4: Item Size Exceeds Limit

**Error:** `ItemSizeLimitExceeded` (max 400 KB per item)

**Solution:**
```bash
# Split large items into multiple items
# Use reference pattern:
# Main item: {"user_id": "user-123", "data_size": "large"}
# Related items: {"user_id#details": "user-123#part1", "content": "..."}

# Query related items separately

# Store large data in S3, reference in DynamoDB
{
  "user_id": "user-123",
  "s3_bucket": "my-bucket",
  "s3_key": "large-file.json"
}
```

